-- title:
--   Counting τ-stable cyclic subgroups of order n in (ℤ/n)²
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a natural number, nonzero, and let $\tau$ be an additive endomorphism of $(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}) \times (\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z})$ satisfying $\tau(\tau v) + \tau v + v = 0$ for every $v$, that is, $\tau^2 + \tau + 1 = 0$ as an endomorphism. Assume further that for every prime $p$ dividing $n$ there is an element $v$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z})^2$ of additive order exactly $p$ such that $\tau v \neq k \cdot v$ for every natural number $k$; thus $\tau$ acts non-scalarly on the $p$-torsion for each prime divisor $p$ of $n$. The conclusion is an equality of cardinalities: the number of additive subgroups $H$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z})^2$ that are cyclic, have cardinality $n$, and satisfy $H.\mathrm{map}\,\tau = H$ (the image of $H$ under $\tau$ is $H$ itself), equals $\nu_3(n)$, which by definition is the number of elements $x$ of $\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}$ with $x^2 + x + 1 = 0$.
--
--   This is the arithmetic core of the count of elliptic points of order three (those lying above $j = 0$) on the modular curve $Y_0(N)$: cyclic subgroups of order $N$ stable under an automorphism of order three of the underlying group of torsion points correspond to roots of $x^2+x+1$ modulo $N$. It is used by the transport of the same count to an abstract abelian group whose $n$-torsion is $(\mathbb{Z}/n)^2$, and by the formulae counting orbits of the subgroups generated by $S$ and by $ST$ acting on the $\Gamma_0$-coset space.
-- source:
